1
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,760
Come on, come on!

2
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:13,080
Where are you training? Get more gear.

3
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,880
You two brothers never lose, huh?

4
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:30,880
Hey, let's celebrate
for my little brother!

5
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:43,400
-Arm!
-Arm!

6
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,560
<i>Getting to this day was so damn hard.</i>

7
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:00,440
<i>Growing up on the streets</i>
<i>and making it this far,</i>

8
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:02,120
<i>I never even dared to dream about it.</i>

9
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,480
<i>This massive explosion</i>

10
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:17,480
<i>caused the fire to spread rapidly,</i>
<i>overwhelming the authorities' ability</i>

11
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,280
<i>to rescue everyone.</i>

12
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:24,400
<i>One body after another</i>
<i>was recovered from the sea of flames.</i>

13
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:28,360
<i>Most of the victims were women</i>
<i>living in a dormitory building</i>

14
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:31,440
<i>located beside the road</i>
<i>where the gas truck overturned.</i>

15
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:35,080
<i>Many others were people trapped</i>
<i>inside the dozens of vehicles nearby.</i>

16
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,120
Hey, are you nervous?

17
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,080
Of course.

18
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:58,440
You see this?

19
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,920
"Man Ocean"?

20
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,040
There's nothing here.

21
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,160
Go check the odds.

22
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,240
Whoa.

23
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,320
Five to two?

24
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:21,000
Damn, the guy who sets the odds

25
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:23,400
is treating me
like some street-fighting boxer.

26
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,840
The real thing isn't in the betting odds.

27
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,600
You're gonna win no matter what.

28
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,040
Have I ever let you down?

29
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,160
Hey.

30
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:40,000
Hey. Don't even think about it. Never.

31
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,520
-Never!
-Never?

32
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:44,840
Never.

33
00:04:56,120 --> 00:05:00,440
Good, good, good.

34
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,920
Hey.

35
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:06,040
Why are you complaining so much?

36
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,640
&lrm;Come on, Dom.

37
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,480
I'm a temple boy, not a boxer.

38
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:12,400
Are you gonna beat me so bad
I can't even help out at the temple?

39
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,160
Alright, we can stop for today.

40
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,000
That was worth every penny you paid me.

41
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,960
Paid me a hundred, hit like a million.

42
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,640
You beat me so bad
I have to see a joint doctor.

43
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,640
My eye hurts too.

44
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,440
Does it really hurt?

45
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:28,960
Yeah. I'm seeing the doctor.
She's pretty. I'm gonna hit on her.

46
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,680
-She's pretty?
-Yes, Sir.

47
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:33,600
-George!
-Keep moving.

48
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,640
Don't forget my pay, okay?
Pay me all at once tomorrow.

49
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,560
Hey, don't.

50
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,000
I'm all sweaty.

51
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,760
Then I'll go take a shower.

52
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:12,880
I don't want to miss the fight.

53
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:15,800
Wait.

54
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,080
If you had to choose
between the fight and your wife,

55
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,800
who would you choose?

56
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,640
My wife, of course.

57
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:30,800
Weren't you gonna shower
and come back down for the fight?

58
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,760
I told you. If I had to choose
between the fight and my wife,

59
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,080
I'd choose my wife every time.

60
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,160
That's enough.

61
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,280
Mom and Dad are coming.

62
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:04,440
Hurry up and take a shower.

63
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:08,600
Go now. You're covered in sweat.

64
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,680
Alright! Round one is here.

65
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,760
Let's see how it goes.

66
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:32,560
Thank you.

67
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,160
What's up?

68
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:49,880
Of course I'm nervous.

69
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,160
Who would've thought
I'd get to fight at Lumpinee Stadium?

70
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:55,920
Give it your all.

71
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,280
Ring or street, it's the same.

72
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:01,600
You got this.

73
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:10,000
<i>In the red corner, Man Ocean,</i>
<i>the middleweight champion!</i>

74
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:20,240
<i>And in the blue corner,</i>
<i>Arm King, the rising star!</i>

75
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:27,840
Arm is really amazing.

76
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:30,040
King Boxing Camp just opened not long ago.

77
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,840
He's already fighting for a title
on the big stage.

78
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,159
Don't you want to join a boxing camp?

79
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:38,039
You could fight for a championship too.

80
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:38,960
No.

81
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:42,159
Boxing camps want all their fighters
to eat and sleep there.

82
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:44,640
That's okay. I'm fine with that.

83
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,560
But I'm not.

84
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:52,800
If I lived at a boxing camp,
I wouldn't get to be with you.

85
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:57,000
That's why you just keep living off her.

86
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:06,160
Look, I bought you lots of food.

87
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:11,840
Come on, Mom. I'll help.

88
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,960
Oh, Mom.

89
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:17,920
I bought you new slippers too.

90
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:21,880
-Let me see.
-Ditch the old pair. Wear these.

91
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,440
-Okay.
-Do you like them?

92
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:26,320
I do. Thank you so much, dear.

93
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,800
-I'll go change them for you.
-Okay.

94
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:32,160
Come on, Dom. Help me serve the food.

95
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,640
Yes.

96
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,600
How long can a boxer make a living?

97
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,320
Don't mind him.

98
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:06,240
I know you love Fon.

99
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:13,040
I'm on your side, and I'm cheering you on.

100
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,000
Good!

101
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,240
Hey, stay calm!

102
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,200
Hit him!

103
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,120
Stay calm, Arm! The round's almost over.

104
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,520
-Get back to your corner.
-Come here.

105
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:53,640
You okay? Spit out your mouthguard.

106
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:55,880
Bucket, quick.

107
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,920
Listen to me!

108
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,600
Protect your body.
Keep your guard up and find your opening.

109
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:08,440
Then go for his face. Got it?

110
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,920
You got this.

111
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,360
-I got this.
-You got this.

112
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,320
I got this.

113
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,120
THAI BOXING FEDERATION

114
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,240
Arm.

115
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,320
Knock his ass out.

116
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:50,920
Fight!

117
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,320
-Don't rush!
-Don't rush!

118
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,200
-Get him!
-Come on!

119
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,400
Don't drop your guard!

120
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,160
Good!

121
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:22,800
To the champion!

122
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:26,360
This is for everyone!

123
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,280
Yeah.

124
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:29,120
Let's share this drink.

125
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,600
Sure.

126
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:34,800
You're the best!

127
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,000
To you, Arm.

128
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:39,640
-Whoa.
-Come on.

129
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,200
Save some for me too.

130
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,800
I'll pay you to drink.

131
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:44,560
-I'll pass.
-This is yours.

132
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:46,720
How much did you bet?

133
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,040
I told you.

134
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:51,200
I was sure you were gonna win.

135
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,000
-Win!
-Of course.

136
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,400
Alright!

137
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:04,640
A toast
to the newest middleweight champion!

138
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,760
Bottoms up.

139
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:12,960
-Pong, don't pretend. Drink up.
-No ice in mine.

140
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:14,320
You bastard.

141
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:17,560
Here.

142
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,040
Come on.

143
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:25,960
I think if our boxing camp succeeds,

144
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:29,120
I'll quit the gambling den and bar.

145
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:41,320
And I finally want to do
what I promised her.

146
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,320
It won't be long.

147
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,640
Your King Camp is gonna be the biggest!

148
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:53,160
Really. For real!

149
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:56,280
You're always making me drink.

150
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:57,840
I'm just worried about one thing.

151
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,680
Since we refused to throw the fight,

152
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:03,760
you think Peng's really okay with it?

153
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:11,680
How much do you want?

154
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:13,480
I told you, I'm not throwing the fight.

155
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:16,040
You're gonna lose anyway.
Why are you being so stubborn?

156
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:19,800
You're just afraid your guy will lose,
so you want me to throw.

157
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,840
I already gave you a chance.

158
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:30,640
I gotta say, I'm pretty awesome too.

159
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,040
-Come on!
-Come on.

160
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:36,920
-Bottoms up!
-Cheers!

161
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,680
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

162
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,840
Cheers, Arm. Drink up!

163
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:43,400
-Arm King!
-Arm King!

164
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:46,240
-Arm King!
-Arm King!

165
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:52,800
Miss! Five bottles of beer!

166
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,640
Hey!

167
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:03,640
-Hey!
-Stop!

168
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:06,440
Hey!

169
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,920
-Arm! What's wrong?
-It hurts.

170
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:37,760
Arm.

171
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:42,720
Arm!

172
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:47,760
Hey! Call an ambulance! Now!

173
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,320
Call an ambulance, quick!

174
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:54,480
Stay with me!

175
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:57,440
Arm. Arm!

176
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,440
Arm.

177
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:16,800
Arm.

178
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,440
Arm.

179
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,080
Arm!

180
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:27,720
Arm!

181
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,200
Arm!

182
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:37,360
Arm!

183
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,080
Arm!

184
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:17,080
SIX MONTHS LATER

185
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:35,360
SPECIAL FIGHT - SING KHANONGNA VS DOM STAR
WAT BAN HAET, KHON KAEN

186
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,280
Khon Kaen?

187
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,640
I'm not going.

188
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,840
This guy has never lost a fight.

189
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:48,520
I think he's the one. You gotta see him.

190
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:56,880
DOM STAR - WAT BAN HAET - KHON KAEN

191
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,040
Hey, hello.

192
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:20,600
-Yes?
-Auntie.

193
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:23,880
Hey.

194
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:29,160
Auntie, how much for the shrimp?

195
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:34,840
Look at her.

196
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,880
Hey, girl.

197
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,640
-Hey!
-What school do you go to?

198
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:44,000
-Hey, let me give you a ride.
-I'll take you home.

199
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,760
-Let go.
-Come on, I'll take you.

200
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:47,560
-Let me go!
-Hey, what the hell?

201
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:49,680
Go after her!

202
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:50,640
Get her!

203
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:53,720
Hey!

204
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,960
-Don't run!
-Hey!

205
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:57,640
Stop right there!

206
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:00,320
Hey!

207
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:05,800
Hey, where you going?

208
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,360
You're fast, huh?

209
00:21:12,840 --> 00:21:14,560
You're not getting away this time.

210
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:47,880
Are you okay?

211
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,960
I'm okay. Thank you.

212
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:16,000
Smells so good.

213
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:18,200
It's just an omelet.

214
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,600
Something going on?

215
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:32,120
I'm not going to cheer for you today.

216
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:37,120
I knew it. You're acting sweet
because something's up.

217
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:40,440
Why? Busy with work?

218
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:52,720
I have to handle my transfer.

219
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:56,040
Transfer?

220
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,440
Transfer where?

221
00:23:04,760 --> 00:23:05,960
Bangkok.

222
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:18,000
When did you find out about this?

223
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:20,640
A month ago.

224
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:24,480
And you didn't think about telling me?

225
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:29,880
My dad talked to his friend
at the Crime Suppression Division.

226
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:35,440
They were looking for a sharpshooter,
so he suggested my name.

227
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:39,400
And they chose you.

228
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:51,600
Why are you only telling me today?

229
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:59,440
Because I'm about to move soon.

230
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:02,920
Soon means when?

231
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:08,160
Fon, when is it?

232
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:14,360
Next week.

233
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:28,640
Why didn't you tell me?

234
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:30,880
I knew you wouldn't be okay with it.

235
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:32,840
I wasn't the one who decided this.

236
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:34,360
Even if I told you, nothing would change.

237
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:35,560
Fon.

238
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:39,360
But shouldn't I at least know
that my wife is moving to Bangkok?

239
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:42,160
Shouldn't I know when you're leaving,
how long you'll be gone?

240
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:44,840
What about us, Fon?

241
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:47,360
By us, I mean the two of us.

242
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:51,520
I know.

243
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:55,120
I just didn't want to go against my dad.

244
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:03,000
I know your dad doesn't like me

245
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:06,440
because I'm just a lousy boxer

246
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:08,360
fighting at temple fairs.

247
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:11,720
That's not it.

248
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:14,920
I've never minded you being a boxer.

249
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:23,080
But my dad…

250
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:34,640
Forget it.

251
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:39,040
Let's just say you've told me now.

252
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:43,880
We just have to figure out

253
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:46,360
what we're going to do next.

254
00:25:58,800 --> 00:26:00,280
Thank you.

255
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:30,600
-Hey, Oab.
-Yeah?

256
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:32,800
I'm gonna go buy some grilled meatballs.
Want anything?

257
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:33,920
No, you go ahead.

258
00:26:49,560 --> 00:26:51,600
Two baht per stick.

259
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:05,160
Are you done yet?

260
00:27:08,800 --> 00:27:10,400
Hurry up. We're gonna miss it.

261
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:16,280
They haven't started fighting yet.

262
00:27:16,360 --> 00:27:19,080
I know,
but we won't get a spot in the front.

263
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:23,600
Alright, let's go.

264
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:26,360
When we grow up,
I'll open a boxing camp for you.

265
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,040
Yeah.

266
00:27:37,600 --> 00:27:40,000
Hello, everyone.

267
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:43,840
Please come watch our fighters today.

268
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:47,280
In the blue corner, Dom Star!

269
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:54,040
And now, let's welcome Sing Khanongna!

270
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:55,960
He's done for!

271
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:57,680
Red corner! Blue corner!

272
00:27:58,320 --> 00:27:59,360
Fighter!

273
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:00,960
Hey!

274
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:02,960
<i>I have to handle my transfer.</i>

275
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:04,920
Next week.

276
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:06,520
Fighter!

277
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:11,680
Whoa.

278
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:16,920
-Hey. He's calling you.
-Huh?

279
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:17,920
Huh?

280
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:21,440
Even my rooster's more awake than you.

281
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:23,000
The referee's calling you.

282
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:26,440
What's wrong with him?

283
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:31,160
Fight with all you've got.
Show good sportsmanship.

284
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:32,640
Follow my orders strictly.

285
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:34,720
Fight!

286
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,400
<i>-Transfer where?</i>
<i>-Bangkok.</i>

287
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:54,800
<i>I didn't want to go against my dad.</i>

288
00:28:57,400 --> 00:28:59,280
What's he doing?

289
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:14,760
-Whoa!
-Get up!

290
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:17,960
-Get up!
-Hurry!

291
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:20,080
-Get up!
-Wake up!

292
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:22,760
-See you at the hotel.
-Get up!

293
00:29:22,840 --> 00:29:24,320
Get up!

294
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:26,200
Come on! Get up!

295
00:29:26,280 --> 00:29:27,600
Get up!

296
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:30,080
-Get up!
-Five, six.

297
00:29:30,160 --> 00:29:32,120
Seven, eight…

298
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:18,400
Mom.

299
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:22,200
-Mom.
-Take good care of each other.

300
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:25,000
Mom.

301
00:30:25,520 --> 00:30:27,520
Oab, look after your brother.

302
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:28,760
Yes.

303
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:36,880
Mom.

304
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:47,200
Take good care of each other, okay?

305
00:30:47,280 --> 00:30:48,760
-Mom!
-Mom.

306
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:31,040
Where did he go?

307
00:31:52,760 --> 00:31:53,960
Thank you, Auntie.

308
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:05,880
Where have you been?

309
00:32:07,560 --> 00:32:09,200
Where have you been?

310
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:13,520
Just went for a walk.

311
00:32:13,600 --> 00:32:14,840
Where?

312
00:32:14,920 --> 00:32:16,280
Around your house?

313
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:24,440
Wasn't it enough to just watch
the temple fair fighter like I said?

314
00:32:24,520 --> 00:32:26,560
I didn't want to come in the first place.

315
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:31,120
But part of you wanted to come, didn't it?

316
00:32:32,320 --> 00:32:33,800
What more do you want from me?

317
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:37,120
I didn't want to come. You forced me to.

318
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:38,280
And now that I'm here,

319
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:41,480
that so-called great fighter
is freaking terrible.

320
00:32:42,840 --> 00:32:43,920
You wasted my time.

321
00:32:45,120 --> 00:32:46,400
What else do you want from me?

322
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:50,760
Go get some sleep.

323
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:52,480
We have to go to Bangkok early tomorrow.

324
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:04,040
How's your father?

325
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:06,040
He's doing well.

326
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:09,920
Your father and I have been close
since we were at the police cadet academy.

327
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:13,840
He called me and asked

328
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:15,440
if I could find an open position for you.

329
00:33:17,280 --> 00:33:19,800
Luckily, we needed a sharpshooter here,

330
00:33:19,880 --> 00:33:20,960
so we called you in.

331
00:33:21,600 --> 00:33:22,720
Yes.

332
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:30,720
Your boyfriend is a boxer?

333
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:32,720
Yes.

334
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:35,160
Are you moving to Bangkok together?

335
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:39,400
He's looking for a job right now.
Once he finds one, he'll move here.

336
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:42,120
Then for now,

337
00:33:42,200 --> 00:33:44,360
stay at the police housing, okay?

338
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:48,240
Yes. Once he moves here,
we'll find a place.

339
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:56,440
Oab spent a week in Khon Kaen.
Why's he so quiet?

340
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:58,160
Thought you said that boxer was good.

341
00:33:59,200 --> 00:34:00,880
Good? Not even close.

342
00:34:01,600 --> 00:34:04,560
I didn't even finish my meatball skewer
before he went down.

343
00:34:04,640 --> 00:34:05,720
-Seriously?
-Yeah.

344
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:07,280
People said he'd never lost, didn't they?

345
00:34:08,239 --> 00:34:09,280
Just rumors.

346
00:34:09,880 --> 00:34:12,040
How about this? Let him give it a try.

347
00:34:12,120 --> 00:34:13,199
Maybe he's got potential.

348
00:34:14,239 --> 00:34:17,360
Ever since Arm died,
the boxing camp's been completely dead.

349
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:19,960
-Hey, guys.
-Oh, hey, Oab.

350
00:34:21,040 --> 00:34:22,880
Thought you weren't coming.

351
00:34:23,800 --> 00:34:24,800
Nothing to do at home.

352
00:34:25,719 --> 00:34:26,760
How's the bar?

353
00:34:27,639 --> 00:34:29,880
The bar's doing good.
I'll show you the accounts.

354
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:32,679
Just the same old people
asking you for money.

355
00:34:36,280 --> 00:34:38,320
I already know who.

356
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:52,600
Have you heard anything about Peng?

357
00:34:57,360 --> 00:35:00,440
<i>My guys say Peng's being careful.</i>
<i>He's always got his men with him.</i>

358
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:04,400
<i>There's no opening.</i>
<i>Liang stays right by Peng's side.</i>

359
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:05,680
<i>Getting close to him is really hard.</i>

360
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:06,760
NOW HIRING - ONE SERVER POSITION

361
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:08,520
The motive is so obvious.

362
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:10,000
Peng ordered Arm's murder,

363
00:35:10,720 --> 00:35:11,920
but he's still walking free.

364
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,440
Those bastards all know.

365
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:24,840
If the people responsible for justice
can't do their job,

366
00:35:26,240 --> 00:35:28,360
then it's time for us to take action.

367
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,000
I agree.

368
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:34,880
You've let Peng think
he can do anything to us for too long.

369
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:38,840
If you're going after Peng,

370
00:35:39,960 --> 00:35:41,760
you have to get Liang first.

371
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:48,160
Good. They're not getting back up.

372
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:52,440
I saw them looking for a boxer before,

373
00:35:52,520 --> 00:35:53,840
but lately they've gone quiet.

374
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:56,440
I guess they couldn't find anyone
as good as their old guy.

375
00:35:56,520 --> 00:35:59,120
I remember. I lost millions on that match.

376
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:05,920
It's better if he quits.
That guy is stubborn.

377
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:08,720
He left me
because he refused to sell my drugs.

378
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:11,200
I don't care
if he opens a bar or a gambling den.

379
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:14,960
But refusing to take a fall for me?
That's where I draw the line.

380
00:36:17,040 --> 00:36:19,240
I just had a problem with his bar.

381
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:20,720
What now?

382
00:36:21,240 --> 00:36:22,720
He's selling illegal liquor, Boss.

383
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:24,320
We sell it too.

384
00:36:24,400 --> 00:36:27,480
But we agreed
we'd sell it at the legal price.

385
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,440
He's undercutting us?

386
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:37,880
What do you want to do?

387
00:37:13,040 --> 00:37:14,080
Thank you.

388
00:37:17,240 --> 00:37:17,920
NOW HIRING

389
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:20,600
When will I finally get a job?

390
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:22,280
NOW HIRING - STAFF WANTED

391
00:37:27,480 --> 00:37:28,600
Hello.

392
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:29,680
<i>I'm here.</i>

393
00:37:33,480 --> 00:37:34,680
Did you report in already?

394
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,280
I miss you.

395
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:47,800
The room feels empty without you.

396
00:37:50,760 --> 00:37:53,880
Just wait for me, okay?
Once I find a job, I'll come join you.

397
00:37:54,680 --> 00:37:56,480
Couldn't you come here first
and look for one?

398
00:37:57,760 --> 00:38:00,240
Your dad already thinks
I'm living off you.

399
00:38:00,320 --> 00:38:03,600
If I go there without a job,
he'll think even worse.

400
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:11,840
Love you.

401
00:38:13,120 --> 00:38:15,200
I'll go tidy up the room.

402
00:38:16,680 --> 00:38:17,640
Love you too.

403
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:00,040
Still miss me?

404
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:22,520
I'm here to apply for a job.

405
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:26,000
What did you say?

406
00:39:27,400 --> 00:39:28,640
I'm here to apply for a job.

407
00:39:28,720 --> 00:39:30,320
Alright, sit down.

408
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:31,920
Have a seat.

409
00:39:41,720 --> 00:39:43,000
Let me see your resume.

410
00:39:51,040 --> 00:39:52,160
You box too?

411
00:39:52,840 --> 00:39:55,680
Yes. I've never done anything else.

412
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:58,600
Dom from Khon Kaen.

413
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:02,320
You're Dom Star?

414
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:05,080
Yes.

415
00:40:05,640 --> 00:40:06,640
You still fighting?

416
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:10,560
-No, I quit.
-Why?

417
00:40:15,040 --> 00:40:16,040
My wife passed away.

418
00:40:17,280 --> 00:40:18,120
I see.

419
00:40:18,840 --> 00:40:19,880
Where are you staying now?

420
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:21,920
I don't have a place yet.

421
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:23,640
When can you start?

422
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:26,920
If you hire me, I can start right away.

423
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:31,720
Then start today.

424
00:40:31,800 --> 00:40:34,480
Go stock the liquor in the back.
Follow me.

425
00:40:35,200 --> 00:40:37,080
<i>I have a favor to ask.</i>

426
00:40:37,880 --> 00:40:39,280
<i>This is confidential.</i>

427
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:41,760
You can't tell anyone, not even your wife.

428
00:40:43,360 --> 00:40:44,920
What do I have to do?

429
00:40:45,520 --> 00:40:47,000
You'll have to work for me.

430
00:40:47,080 --> 00:40:49,080
Go undercover and join Oab's group.

431
00:40:51,080 --> 00:40:52,520
Who is Oab?

432
00:40:54,080 --> 00:40:56,160
He is an influential figure

433
00:40:56,240 --> 00:40:58,880
we suspect may be involved
in drug trafficking.

434
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:04,080
And what do I get?

435
00:41:05,240 --> 00:41:06,600
What do you want?

436
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:09,920
Security.

437
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:13,920
If you solve this case,

438
00:41:14,520 --> 00:41:17,440
I'll make you a police-affiliated boxer.

439
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:22,680
<i>You'll get a rank, a salary, and benefits.</i>
<i>Is that enough?</i>

440
00:41:25,160 --> 00:41:27,040
<i>But you need to get evidence</i>
<i>to arrest Oab.</i>

441
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:28,960
Proof he's trafficking drugs.

442
00:41:34,480 --> 00:41:35,320
Boss.

443
00:41:36,120 --> 00:41:36,960
What is it?

444
00:41:37,560 --> 00:41:38,440
Well…

445
00:41:39,240 --> 00:41:42,280
Can I sleep at the bar?
I still haven't found a place to stay.

446
00:41:43,720 --> 00:41:45,200
Shouldn't be a problem.

447
00:41:45,720 --> 00:41:46,760
I'll ask them for you.

448
00:41:48,480 --> 00:41:49,440
Come on.

449
00:41:56,920 --> 00:41:58,480
NOW HIRING - ONE SERVER POSITION

450
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:08,320
Excuse me.

451
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:11,640
Your ice.

452
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:15,640
Hey, this place has cheap drinks.

453
00:42:15,720 --> 00:42:17,000
-Bring it over.
-Yes.

454
00:42:17,600 --> 00:42:19,080
-Make it quick.
-Yes.

455
00:42:19,160 --> 00:42:20,280
Cheers.

456
00:42:31,160 --> 00:42:32,760
Hi there. What can I get you?

457
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:34,520
The usual shots?

458
00:42:34,600 --> 00:42:35,760
How many shots so far?

459
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:37,720
Enjoy your drink.

460
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:43,600
-Oh, hey!
-Hey, bro.

461
00:42:43,680 --> 00:42:45,040
Pretty lively tonight.

462
00:42:45,120 --> 00:42:46,720
Packed. Really packed.

463
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:47,960
It's going pretty well.

464
00:42:49,680 --> 00:42:50,520
New guy, huh?

465
00:42:50,600 --> 00:42:52,400
Yeah. I forgot to tell you.

466
00:42:52,480 --> 00:42:53,920
I hired a new guy.

467
00:43:05,920 --> 00:43:07,320
The place is packed tonight, damn it.

468
00:43:12,920 --> 00:43:14,720
Why did you do that to my guy?

469
00:43:15,240 --> 00:43:16,480
Illegal liquor, huh?

470
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:18,080
No wonder it's so cheap.

471
00:43:18,720 --> 00:43:20,320
Yours isn't illegal, I guess?

472
00:43:21,120 --> 00:43:23,240
You sell liquor this cheap,

473
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:26,400
so everyone comes here.
You're killing the other bars.

474
00:43:26,480 --> 00:43:29,280
I'll sell at whatever price I want.

475
00:43:29,360 --> 00:43:31,000
If other bars can't match it,

476
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:33,720
that's their problem, not mine.

477
00:43:34,440 --> 00:43:35,640
Your brother died,

478
00:43:36,520 --> 00:43:38,760
and your boxing camp
still hasn't recovered.

479
00:43:39,800 --> 00:43:41,640
If you don't want anyone else dying,

480
00:43:42,240 --> 00:43:43,840
match everyone else's prices.

481
00:44:02,880 --> 00:44:03,760
Come here!

482
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:42,440
What the hell does my brother's death
have to do with you?

483
00:45:42,520 --> 00:45:44,360
Please don't do anything to me.

484
00:45:44,880 --> 00:45:46,240
I'm begging you.

485
00:45:46,960 --> 00:45:48,280
Please don't do anything to me.

486
00:45:52,480 --> 00:45:54,360
Your boss killed my little brother.

487
00:45:57,960 --> 00:45:58,880
Please.

488
00:46:01,080 --> 00:46:02,280
Please don't do anything to me.

489
00:46:05,920 --> 00:46:08,400
Were you the one who gave them the tip?

490
00:46:15,840 --> 00:46:16,960
What tip?

491
00:46:18,440 --> 00:46:19,920
You just started working here today,

492
00:46:21,040 --> 00:46:23,400
and this bastard showed up
right when I was at the bar.

493
00:46:26,440 --> 00:46:28,000
Someone must've tipped him off.

494
00:46:42,640 --> 00:46:44,040
If you're not working with him, then…

495
00:46:46,600 --> 00:46:47,560
Here.

496
00:47:12,960 --> 00:47:13,960
If it wasn't you,

497
00:47:14,960 --> 00:47:16,240
kill him.

498
00:49:01,200 --> 00:49:02,520
Boxer, come with me.

499
00:49:55,040 --> 00:49:56,480
Boss, Oab is here.

500
00:50:01,160 --> 00:50:02,200
Hey.

501
00:50:05,880 --> 00:50:07,080
He's your guy, isn't he?

502
00:50:07,160 --> 00:50:08,880
Boss, help me.

503
00:50:13,360 --> 00:50:14,640
Please help me.

504
00:50:15,240 --> 00:50:16,320
I don't know him.

505
00:50:21,320 --> 00:50:22,560
You sure

506
00:50:23,120 --> 00:50:24,920
you didn't send someone to my bar?

507
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:26,640
Did he tell you

508
00:50:26,720 --> 00:50:28,920
he works for me?

509
00:50:31,040 --> 00:50:32,360
Boss.

510
00:50:33,120 --> 00:50:34,560
Boss, don't!

511
00:50:42,320 --> 00:50:46,280
Now he's not my guy anymore.

512
00:50:48,760 --> 00:50:50,640
Got a problem with that?

513
00:50:55,320 --> 00:50:57,400
I know you killed my brother.

514
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:04,920
Where? Where's your proof?

515
00:51:05,560 --> 00:51:06,400
Huh?

516
00:51:06,920 --> 00:51:08,520
You don't have any.

517
00:51:09,160 --> 00:51:12,440
No proof means I didn't do it.

518
00:51:14,080 --> 00:51:17,320
And if I did, I'd be in prison by now.

519
00:51:32,600 --> 00:51:35,040
Boss, Mr. Suthep is here.

520
00:52:06,480 --> 00:52:08,240
You're lucky today.

521
00:52:16,400 --> 00:52:18,800
-Take care of it.
-Yes.

522
00:52:56,040 --> 00:52:57,680
That damn Peng won't quit.

523
00:52:59,960 --> 00:53:03,000
If we don't hit back,
he'll keep coming after you.

524
00:53:09,040 --> 00:53:10,520
-Dum.
-Yeah?

525
00:53:11,440 --> 00:53:14,760
Don't take the repair money from the bar.
I'll pay for it.

526
00:53:14,840 --> 00:53:16,720
It's fine.
The bar's still making a profit.

527
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:17,880
We can cover it.

528
00:53:17,960 --> 00:53:20,920
No, it's fine. Come get it from me.

529
00:53:22,800 --> 00:53:24,320
-I'm leaving.
-Alright.

530
00:53:26,040 --> 00:53:27,480
Dom, stay and watch the bar tonight.

531
00:53:27,560 --> 00:53:28,400
Yes.

532
00:53:34,360 --> 00:53:36,040
I'll sleep here with you.

533
00:53:36,120 --> 00:53:39,480
With things like this happening,
it's risky for you to be alone.

534
00:53:43,400 --> 00:53:44,560
I probably won't sleep anyway.

535
00:53:57,240 --> 00:53:58,600
Did you have someone clean it up?

536
00:53:59,200 --> 00:54:00,280
It's taken care of, Boss.

537
00:54:01,200 --> 00:54:02,880
Don't let this come back to me.

538
00:54:03,440 --> 00:54:04,320
Yes.

539
00:54:07,800 --> 00:54:09,040
Honestly,

540
00:54:09,920 --> 00:54:12,160
Mr. Suthep shouldn't have shown up today.

541
00:54:13,520 --> 00:54:15,600
They came to us. We could've handled them.

542
00:54:18,880 --> 00:54:22,000
Come to think of it, they've got guts.

543
00:54:22,640 --> 00:54:24,240
They came straight to us.

544
00:54:24,840 --> 00:54:28,080
That's why I said
we can't leave them alone for too long.

545
00:54:28,160 --> 00:54:30,040
If we let them,

546
00:54:30,800 --> 00:54:32,680
they'll walk all over us.

547
00:54:34,560 --> 00:54:37,680
After his brother died,
I thought he had quit.

548
00:54:37,760 --> 00:54:39,120
What are you going to do about him?

549
00:54:39,200 --> 00:54:42,200
Not yet. Tomorrow, go get more supplies.

550
00:54:42,280 --> 00:54:44,400
We won't have enough to sell otherwise.

551
00:54:54,800 --> 00:54:56,680
If he'd agreed to sell for me,

552
00:54:57,200 --> 00:54:59,120
none of this fighting would've happened.

553
00:55:03,760 --> 00:55:05,600
You have a delivery tomorrow, right?

554
00:55:05,680 --> 00:55:06,680
Yes.

555
00:55:07,600 --> 00:55:09,600
Then I'll have someone else handle it.

556
00:55:10,120 --> 00:55:12,960
You go get the supplies for me first.

557
00:55:13,560 --> 00:55:14,480
Yes, Boss.

558
00:56:20,920 --> 00:56:22,040
-Hey.
-Harder!

559
00:56:22,120 --> 00:56:23,000
Spar with me for a round.

560
00:56:32,040 --> 00:56:33,760
I don't trust this guy.

561
00:56:33,840 --> 00:56:34,840
Aren't you overthinking this?

562
00:56:35,760 --> 00:56:37,480
I've never seen you trust anyone.

563
00:56:37,560 --> 00:56:39,640
Sir, I'm at the boxing camp now.

564
00:56:50,440 --> 00:56:51,480
Dom!

565
00:56:58,360 --> 00:56:59,320
It's Dom.

566
00:57:00,520 --> 00:57:01,680
Who's he meeting?

567
00:57:04,040 --> 00:57:06,120
-Fon?
-Oab?

568
00:57:40,480 --> 00:57:41,360
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
